{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension","id":1035897,"title":"Advice on how to port a Mage: The Awakening hombrew to Ascension.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-21T17:11:38-08:00","id":1035897,"title":"Advice on how to port a Mage: The Awakening hombrew to Ascension.","content":"A while ago I came up with a Homebrew on The Onyx Path Forums. It was basically a antagonist idea for Mage: The Awakening called Project Prometheus, a scientific organization dedicated to studying Magical Artifacts thinking they are a way to unlock the 90% of our brains we don't use. They viewed Mages as Psychics and believed that finding Atlantis would be the key to becoming like them. Here is a link to the thread if you need more information. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1008958-an-idea-for-mage\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-idea-for-mage</a><br /> <br /> I want to know how I could transfer this to Mage the Ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T03:41:40-08:00","id":1036010,"title":"","content":"This sounds like a group of Etherites.<br /> I don't see how they would be an antagonist to Mage the Ascension style Mages since Atlantis was never really emphasised for us. Though it probably exists somewhere, either in the umbra or in the hollow world.<br /> <br /> If you're trying to have a group of scientists go against the Mages, well, we already have the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:07:07-08:00","id":1036047,"title":"","content":"Well, I know Atlantis does not exist in this world and can cut that part out. Project Prometheus in Mage: TAW was not overtly hostile to Mages, just very interested in them and wanted to figure out scientifically how their so-called magic works and how to unlock it. I can see the Technocracy either ignoring them or doing everything in their power to sabotage their experiments. Besides, they steal artifacts most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:15:00-08:00","id":1036049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036047#post1036047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I know Atlantis does not exist in this world and can cut that part out. Project Prometheus in Mage: TAW was not overtly hostile to Mages, just very interested in them and wanted to figure out scientifically how their so-called magic works and how to unlock it. I can see the Technocracy either ignoring them or doing everything in their power to sabotage their experiments. Besides, they steal artifacts most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which faction of the technocracy.<br /> You can certainly have a progenitor group who are interested in how Mages do their magic and focus on figuring out how their brains differ from the masses. <br /> Similarly you could have a group from Iteration X study them so they may mimic their brain activity with cybernetic AI programmes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:17:13-08:00","id":1036050,"title":"","content":"If they're normal humans peeking the affairs of the Awakened, they might get some attention of technocrats and even some traditionalists that want to keep their doings secret. But they probably ain't going to get open hostility.<br /> <br /> There it's a group like that in Mage already. The Arcanum, a society of ocultists that try to discover all the secrets of the supernatural world. This group could be a section of the Arcanum, or be an unrelated albeit similar operation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:22:50-08:00","id":1036054,"title":"","content":"I knew that the Arcanum exists. The difference between them and Prometheus is methodology. The Arcanum probably uses occultic knowledge to study magic while Prometheus uses the Scientific Method. Also, would the whole stealing Magic artifacts thing annoy Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:31:51-08:00","id":1036057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036054#post1036054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew that the Arcanum exists. The difference between them and Prometheus is methodology. The Arcanum probably uses occultic knowledge to study magic while Prometheus uses the Scientific Method. Also, would the whole stealing Magic artifacts thing annoy Mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which artifacts and which mages.<br /> <br /> If you're guys are stealing wonders, the whoever owns those wonders, be it mage, cabal, or chantry, are understandably going to be annoyed by this.<br /> If they are stealing something more important, then it depends who it's important. The Cult of Ecstasy, for example, aren't going to be all that concerned if a Hermetic Orb of Power is removed or if a Sacred Scroll from an Akashic temple is removed.<br /> Similarly, few other mages are going to be bothered if someone steals an Ecstatic's stash of superdrugs.<br /> <br /> Unless it's an artefact which is really powerful, it's unlikely to garner cross-tradition interest. And if it is, there will be enough people trying to claim it for themselves. The Nephandi, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:52:57-08:00","id":1036067,"title":"","content":"If it's superdrugs I bet it would not make it through the night, possibly through two scientists using it to get high. Also, the scientists steal any magical artifacts they can, which most of the time turn out to be either not to be magic or not very powerful. For example, they once stole a jade dragon statue from a Akashic temple while at the same time they realized a book written in Latin by a Hermatic was not magic at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:06:54-08:00","id":1036071,"title":"","content":"Most mages are going to be annoyed that someone entered their houses to steal their stuff, be it magical or not, but it's unlikely they are going to be all murdery with some mortal dabblers doing a bit of thievry, unless the object it's very sacred to the mage.<br /> It's likely that the mage will attemt to retrieve her stuff, and maybe leave a few curses to punish them or try to scare the scientists, to discourage them from stealing more stuff.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum isn't against using the scientific method to study the supernatural (they're mostly human, after all, if they want to examine vampiric blood, chanting in enochian isn't going to help). It's just that they aren't philosophically against more esoteric or unorthodox means of getting data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:11:47-08:00","id":1036076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036071#post1036071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most mages are going to be annoyed that someone entered their houses to steal their stuff, be it magical or not, but it's unlikely they are going to be all murdery with some mortal dabblers doing a bit of thievry, unless the object it's very sacred to the mage.<br /> It's likely that the mage will attemt to retrieve her stuff, and maybe leave a few curses to punish them or try to scare the scientists, to discourage them from stealing more stuff.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum isn't against using the scientific method to study the supernatural (they're mostly human, after all, if they want to examine vampiric blood, chanting in enochian isn't going to help). It's just that they aren't philosophically against more esoteric or unorthodox means of getting data.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPerhaps they could have a cooperative relationship with the Arcanum? They give the Arcanum the artifacts they steal after they are done studying them and the Arcanum give Prometheus their research. Also, what do you think of Prometheus thinking Magic is just humanity unlocking the 90% of their brain being unlocked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:41:09-08:00","id":1036086,"title":"","content":"The way magic works in Ascension is that any framework for magic is good enough, so long as the willworker believes it thoroughly. So if the mage thinks that using magic is all about accessing the hidden potential of their brain through the use of mystic artefacts, then great. That's a paradigm.<br /> <br /> What would other mages think? Depends very much on who you ask. Some Akashic's would be all for the idea of achieving magic via accessing hidden functions of the mind, though some would be against the idea of the 90% thing, stating that this was the wrong way to go about it, that it wasn't about achieving &quot;more&quot; brain function, but about achieving a better &quot;balance&quot; in brain function. How you use the brain is more important than how much your brain is doing.<br /> <br /> Etherites could be all for this as well, and may invent all manner of helmets or tonics to try and &quot;tap in&quot; to this hidden potential. Other's may have dismissed the notion as too convenient to be true, preferring instead their own theories.<br /> <br /> There may be a number of Ecstatics who use drugs specifically because they think it allows them to tap into that hidden brain power, but a lot of them would say it's not about brain, it's about soul and feel, getting in line with the vibes. Other's might say that 10% is too much, and to truly get in touch with the universe you need to stop thinking, use 0% of the brain and become truly unshackled by your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:02:18-08:00","id":1036100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036086#post1036086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way magic works in Ascension is that any framework for magic is good enough, so long as the willworker believes it thoroughly. So if the mage thinks that using magic is all about accessing the hidden potential of their brain through the use of mystic artefacts, then great. That's a paradigm.<br /> <br /> What would other mages think? Depends very much on who you ask. Some Akashic's would be all for the idea of achieving magic via accessing hidden functions of the mind, though some would be against the idea of the 90% thing, stating that this was the wrong way to go about it, that it wasn't about achieving &quot;more&quot; brain function, but about achieving a better &quot;balance&quot; in brain function. How you use the brain is more important than how much your brain is doing.<br /> <br /> Etherites could be all for this as well, and may invent all manner of helmets or tonics to try and &quot;tap in&quot; to this hidden potential. Other's may have dismissed the notion as too convenient to be true, preferring instead their own theories.<br /> <br /> There may be a number of Ecstatics who use drugs specifically because they think it allows them to tap into that hidden brain power, but a lot of them would say it's not about brain, it's about soul and feel, getting in line with the vibes. Other's might say that 10% is too much, and to truly get in touch with the universe you need to stop thinking, use 0% of the brain and become truly unshackled by your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo Project Prometheus' theory about magic being a higher form of thought could actually be plausible? That's nice to know. Also, Project Promethus scientists have actually never studied a living mage before, mostly due to the fact that the scientists are slightly scared of mages. Yet, they still have a obsession over them and have been known to stalk known mages, which has led them to chantries and inevitably caused them to be looted by Prometheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:20:54-08:00","id":1036112,"title":"","content":"In which case they'd most likely be the scientific equivalent of sorcerors. That is, sleepers who do magic which stays within the boundaries of reality. No spheres, no quintessence, no paradox, but very limited effects which cost willpower to perform.<br /> <br /> Whether the technocracy is aware of them or not is up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T09:43:52-08:00","id":1036127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036112#post1036112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which case they'd most likely be the scientific equivalent of sorcerors. That is, sleepers who do magic which stays within the boundaries of reality. No spheres, no quintessence, no paradox, but very limited effects which cost willpower to perform.<br /> <br /> Whether the technocracy is aware of them or not is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAlright. I am not sure about having the Technocracy know about them. I would think that The Technocracy would know about them due to the grip they have on the world. Then again, Prometheus is ran by a scientist who believes in Psychics so they would probably call him a pseudoscientific nut and ignore him. Also, I could picture a scenario where a cabal comes back from a skirmish with Technocrats only to find their chantry completely pillaged and all of their artifacts gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:56:30-08:00","id":1036163,"title":"","content":"The Technocratic Union's knowledge and control are often overstated. Sure, they have fingers in many pies and vast information technologies, but they aren't omniscient. If they were, the Ascension War would have ended long ago. Especially if the group is small and covert, the Technocracy might not know they even exist.<br /> <br /> If they are aware of Project Prometheus, the next thing to deduce is <i>how much</i> they know, which in turn dictates how much they <i>care</i>. If the Union knows their beliefs but not their activities, they may write them off as more crackpots, to be either ignored or made marginalized within the academic community. The Union does not have infinite time, manpower, or resources to go chasing down every fringe group.<br /> <br /> This tune could change if they realize Project Prometheus is going around, stealing superstitionist artifacts. The Union is unhappy enough with the Traditions having such things. But at least they know (in as much a way that any superstitionist could &quot;know&quot; anything) how their stuff works. Random sleepers have no idea what dangers they could bring down on themselves, innocent bystanders, or the Consensus by meddling with forces beyond their ken. Their involvement in the affairs of the larger Ascension War could also cause these sleepers to become full-fledged superstitionists in and of themselves, to either join the Traditions or remain a disconnected thorn in the Union's side. Such things cannot be permitted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:03:54-08:00","id":1036169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036163#post1036163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocratic Union's knowledge and control are often overstated. Sure, they have fingers in many pies and vast information technologies, but they aren't omniscient. If they were, the Ascension War would have ended long ago. Especially if the group is small and covert, the Technocracy might not know they even exist.<br /> <br /> If they are aware of Project Prometheus, the next thing to deduce is <i>how much</i> they know, which in turn dictates how much they <i>care</i>. If the Union knows their beliefs but not their activities, they may write them off as more crackpots, to be either ignored or made marginalized within the academic community. The Union does not have infinite time, manpower, or resources to go chasing down every fringe group.<br /> <br /> This tune could change if they realize Project Prometheus is going around, stealing superstitionist artifacts. The Union is unhappy enough with the Traditions having such things. But at least they know (in as much a way that any superstitionist could &quot;know&quot; anything) how their stuff works. Random sleepers have no idea what dangers they could bring down on themselves, innocent bystanders, or the Consensus by meddling with forces beyond their ken. Their involvement in the affairs of the larger Ascension War could also cause these sleepers to become full-fledged superstitionists in and of themselves, to either join the Traditions or remain a disconnected thorn in the Union's side. Such things cannot be permitted.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's true. I am also wondering what kind of experiments Prometheus could run on supposedly magical artifacts. One suggestion I got on the original Awakening thread was to have a magic detecting device like a PKE meter from Ghostbusters. How do you think that could work in Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:40:27-08:00","id":1036197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036169#post1036169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's true. I am also wondering what kind of experiments Prometheus could run on supposedly magical artifacts. One suggestion I got on the original Awakening thread was to have a magic detecting device like a PKE meter from Ghostbusters. How do you think that could work in Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div>First thing we need to determine. Are these artifacts Capital A Artifacts (as in Wonders with their own magic inherent to them) or are they focus tools that mages use to enforce their will?<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, then you can have them be whatever you want them to be and work however their paradigm states they work. If it's the former, then you need to think about what kind of Wonder it is. Is it a Fetish like from Werewolf which houses a spirit? Does it have its own Arete rank and hold its own Quintessence? Is it awakened (i.e. does it have sentience?).<br /> Also, who made it? What paradigm does it work under? And can anyone use it, or just those who understand and believe it will work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:50:34-08:00","id":1036204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035897-advice-on-how-to-port-a-mage-the-awakening-hombrew-to-ascension?p=1036197#post1036197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First thing we need to determine. Are these artifacts Capital A Artifacts (as in Wonders with their own magic inherent to them) or are they focus tools that mages use to enforce their will?<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, then you can have them be whatever you want them to be and work however their paradigm states they work. If it's the former, then you need to think about what kind of Wonder it is. Is it a Fetish like from Werewolf which houses a spirit? Does it have its own Arete rank and hold its own Quintessence? Is it awakened (i.e. does it have sentience?).<br /> Also, who made it? What paradigm does it work under? And can anyone use it, or just those who understand and believe it will work?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell one artifact they have under current study could be a jade dragon they swiped from a Akashic temple. It has the ability to breath out fire and possibly talk. I have no idea what paradigm that would be. The only part they experienced was the breathing fire part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}